-**The PR is `change_ref`; `change_url` is the forge's own link (decision changed 2026-11-12: `pr_number` removed; before that 2026-11-08: where `change_url` comes from).** The core reads an item's PR from `change_ref` and converts it to a number only for a forge call, through one helper (`prNumber`, `src/core/change-ref.ts`); forge methods keep taking numbers (their parameter is `pr`). The store takes `change_ref` (a string) wherever it took a PR number: the lookup by PR, the adopted-PR input, the manual-push input, the unreviewed-merge input, and the item patch, whose PR field is `change_ref` (string or null) with an optional `change_url`. There is no `pr_number` column or field: the breaking migration `20261112T1200-controller-change-ref-only` (`src/controller/migrations/`) rebuilds `controller_work_items` and `controller_unreviewed_merges` without it on SQLite and MySQL, keeping every row, the `(project, change_ref)` indexes and the unique `(project, change_ref)` key of unreviewed merges under new index names (`<table>_by_<what>`), and points the work item's child tables back at the new table. The old tables stay as `legacy_controller_work_items` and `legacy_controller_unreviewed_merges` until a contract migration removes them (a follow-up issue). An unreviewed merge's `change_ref` no longer has to be a PR number. Run-outcome data keys and log fields named `pr_number` are not the column and keep their names. **`change_url` rule:** a PR the worker or an interactive session opens stores the `url` of outbound's `pr` delivery (`Forge.openPr`, RFC 0015 M7), recorded on the action and applied to the item on `DeliveryCompleted`. When no URL is given (an adopted PR, an older outcome, a broker with no URL), the store derives `https://<label>/pull/<n>` for a GitHub project with a stored label, else null. A later patch never overwrites a stored `change_url` (`COALESCE`). The state change records `change_ref`, the patched field. The lookup by PR matches `change_ref` only (migration 35 and MySQL step 0035 backfilled it from `pr_number`). Solo (SQLite) and enterprise (MySQL) behave the same.
